[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129154,
      "id": "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9623b3b8-4f21-5a21-ba87-ab0e35d547bf",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/0cc6d75a4bbdd4f633e23b998b92e0e820798a68da300d5f2cfe8aec4d4806ae.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-3$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- **II.** $p(0)=3.$\n- **III.** $x=1$ is a root of odd multiplicity.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-3$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-3$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=3$, which means that $p(0)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at the point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "62995940-899d-566a-a021-af496e4f5664",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
