    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "abbd9aa9-0b96-531c-8950-8996564df21a",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/82c6c6d4c3ba2cf53691cf17b4649d7a1c7ee2985df58665e6214979bc89fe04.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x = 0$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n- **II.** $x =-3$ and $x = 1$ are roots of even multiplicity.\n- **III.** $p(x) \u2192 \u221e$ as $x \u2192 \u221e$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph crosses at x=0 (odd multiplicity) and touches/turns at x=-3 and x=1 (even multiplicities). Its right-hand tail rises, giving p(x) tending to positive infinity.",
