  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129154,
      "id": "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0b887bca-448b-5ed4-b420-ca03c767e992",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/82f0f96f35761a4b95c8f7582690a560b8353dc5622d20124b4068c0a86f141b.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=1$ is a simple root.\n- **II.** $x=5$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- **III.** $x=5$ is a simple root.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=1$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=5$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=5$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=5$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
