    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6210de81-51f3-5bc7-a2dc-df9f6a422e61",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/0e38bf9dbe1459de4315fa47211ecb79c9648cb90ec743dd6f1139ce93f5f366.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-5$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- **II.** $p(0)=4.$\n- **III.** $x=2$ is a root of odd multiplicity.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-5$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-5$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=4$, which means that $p(0)=4.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=2$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at the point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
