      ":question/id": "31826836-cf5f-5929-8aec-a0a08d1c61de",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/39632ba43fe167d1242bcf891dba2ad31a9a0bf3f65ac85077a2ff4f5a818b8d.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-2$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- **II.** $p(0)=2.$\n- **III.** $x=1$ is a root of odd multiplicity.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-2$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-2$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=2$, which means that $p(0)=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at the point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a0005293-4f05-5e74-bcc4-3ee22a68ed2c",
