    "question": {
      ":question/id": "619392fa-942f-5df7-a744-44f0441ae4a1",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/cbe5ce8c11be81f17abfc7c0a2903bb6f83d013d206662aadb3370f336bd4ac0.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=4$ is a simple root.\n\n- **II.** $x=0$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n\n- **III.** $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=4$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=0$  has an even multiplicity because at $x=0$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
